<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Chhuikhadan State</h1><p class="st-meta">1750 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Chhuikhadan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small state of Chhattisgarh unusual in being ruled by a line of Vaishnava Bairagi mahants rather than a warrior clan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Chhuikhadan, also called Kondka, was established around 1750 by a Bairagi religious family, whose heads combined the roles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaishnavism">Vaishnava</a> mahant and landholder. It held its lands as a zamindari under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhonsles">Bhonsles</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nagpur-kingdom">Nagpur Kingdom</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nagpur-kingdom">Nagpur Kingdom</a> was annexed, Chhuikhadan became a feudatory state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces</a>, later part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh-feudatory-states">Chhattisgarh States</a> group of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-states-agency">Eastern States Agency</a>. Its ruler, a Mahant with the title of Raja, governed a small territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>-growing villages.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The state acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and on 1 January 1948 was merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces and Berar</a>, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>. Its territory is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chhuikhadan-state.jpg" alt="Chhuikhadan State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Princely_State_of_Chhuikhadan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1750 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chhuikhadan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism (Vaishnava)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Chhattisgarhi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kondka</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1849&amp;focus=chhuikhadan-state" aria-label="Chhuikhadan State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6854 1382 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chhuikhadan State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7174 1638L7364 1602M7174 1638L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7174 1638h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7174 1638h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1849&amp;focus=chhuikhadan-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
